{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/867730-cover-and-vitae","id":867730,"title":"Cover and vitae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-18T12:23:34-07:00","id":867730,"title":"Cover and vitae","content":"Now because of the demon ST guide we know that a demon's cover can grow to be addicted to vitae but my question is, what if it had further effect on the cover? No nothing like using vitae to boost physical attributes or fuel disciplines but rather a quasi ghoul state. What if vitae could halt the aging of a cover as it halts the aging of a mortal? Or if it couldn't normally possibly by spoofing a demon could achieve this effect since no effect occurring would reveal they were not the mortal they claim. Of course if this immortal cover could be kept 'young' via vitae, maintaining the cover the cover itself would still be a challenge that'd require upkeep as details that supported the cover fade, die or are destroyed.<br /> <br /> The reason I am pondering this possibility is simply what if a demon decided the best place to hide from the machine was among vampires? What if the demon decided their cover would be as a ghoul serving a master or an ambitious demon thought to mimic being a vampire itself. Though use of deep cover, show of power and a few tailor made gadgets the demon can possibly pull this off as long as they can keep their cover young. Shuffling their relationships to a new cover every few decades runs the risk of being discovered after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:04:43-07:00","id":867760,"title":"","content":"I would say that their Primium would negate the transformative effects of Vitae. And remember since ghouls aren't fully mortal.. Spoofing very quickly undoes the subterfuge, as the supernatural traits and more importantly eternal longevity are not attributes regular non supernatural folks possess. So that wouldn't work. Spoofing is useful, but there are limits<br /> <br /> Now show of power +gadgets could work, but Spoofing doesn't. The only exception I could think of would be a Lambda of Going Native an d Deep Cover allowing for this to be possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-18-2016, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T16:22:07-07:00","id":867898,"title":"","content":"My point for spoofing was more the body acts human but I admit deep cover or going native would be more sutible than just spoofing.<br /> <br /> Thank you for the input. I honestly felt there were holes in my initial idea (hence my posting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T02:5